#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:5
#: 088edecd0ce449029d591f9f1506bb5e
msgid "Plane BlackBox Logger using ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:7
#: cb9c676f7dd74e6fa674842926ce471d
msgid "BlackBox loggers are commonly used to capture aircraft position, attitude, and speed information on aircraft without an autopilot. Using an autopilot and GPS, an a custom version of ArduPilot Plane firmware, such a logger can be implemented. Compass is not required, and usually not recommended, or at least disabled, due to possible magnetic interference since the logger position may be close to power wiring in the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:10
#: 02e7bb42ea034982acbc5aca426f76ff
msgid "The firmware can be obtained for any ArduPilot supported autopilot by using the `Custom Firmware Build Server <https://custom.ardupilot.org>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:12
#: f372e0de463e4550bbd4496449d44908
msgid "The default options for the autopilot can be left enabled, and just the enable the Plane:blackbox logging check box and build and then flash to the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:16
#: 54a05d095f454c3c9b0d5e94e278794c
msgid "The GPS should be configured, and all the normal setup calibrations should be done as if it were a normal plane autopilot. However, it will not have any outputs functions, or servos/motors attached. It merely \"rides along\" to record information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:18
#: 35a48e599fcc4365834ad92cb2ea5dfb
msgid "In order to function properly, it will need to auto arm itself in the air."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:20
#: 829d422e2ea34657a07bc011972bf346
msgid "The ``BBOX_SPD`` parameter should be set to a speed in meters/second when the arming will occur after the vehicle is launched and flying, . Default is 5m/s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:22
#: 3cb392fa5c5c4b75b805c3857716e2be
msgid "Logs collected can be downloaded from the SD card after the flight. See :ref:`common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-blackboxlogger.rst:24
#: 2c0455caedc64a3da65f18d3196d22b2
msgid "while not required, it is possible to route the aircraft's power system through the autopilot's power monitor, if one is attached, to log current and voltage also. Likewise, an airspeed sensor could be attached to the logger to record actual airspeed instead of only ground speed. Estimated airspeed and wind speed will be logged, even if no airspeed sensor is used."
msgstr ""
